    "hebrew-next-word": "Hebrew sentence, empty prefix, next word predicted from context.",
    "code-switch": "Hebrew sentence with a Latin-script word mid-sentence, or the return to Hebrew right after one.",
    "missing-apostrophe": "English contraction typed without the apostrophe.",
    "typo": "Plausible slip with a real intended word.",
    "no-correct": "Short or already-correct input where changing it is the failure.",
    "wrong-layout": "A word entered under the wrong layout, using the standard Hebrew/QWERTY key mapping, so it arrives as gibberish in the other script. On a phone this reaches the field by paste or by carrying desktop muscle memory over. Included because it is a familiar Israeli failure, not because stock iOS handles it; expect these to be uncaptured or unhelped."
